§ `Short names of the kinds of decision`

`k a` MEANS `(a) security, neutrality, diplomatic protection or other foreign affairs`
`k b` MEANS `(b) ordinary naturalisation`
`k c1` MEANS `(c)(1) foreigners law: entry`
`k c2` MEANS `(c)(2) foreigners law: a permit`
`k c3` MEANS `(c)(3) foreigners law: provisional admission`
`k c4` MEANS `(c)(4) foreigners law: expulsion under Art 121(2) of the Federal Constitution, or removal`
`k c5` MEANS `(c)(5) foreigners law: deviation from the admission requirements`
`k c6` MEANS `(c)(6) foreigners law: cross-border commuters and travel papers for stateless foreigners`
`k d1` MEANS `(d)(1) asylum: decision of the Federal Administrative Court`
`k d2` MEANS `(d)(2) asylum: decision of a cantonal lower instance on a permit`
`k e` MEANS `(e) refusal to authorise prosecution of members of authorities or federal staff`
`k f` MEANS `(f) public procurement`
`k fbis` MEANS `(fbis) Federal Administrative Court decision on an order under Art 32i of the Passenger Transport Act`
`k g` MEANS `(g) public-law employment`
`k h` MEANS `(h) international administrative assistance`
`k i` MEANS `(i) military, civilian and civil protection service`
`k j` MEANS `(j) economic national supply in severe shortages`
`k k` MEANS `(k) subsidies to which there is no claim`
`k l` MEANS `(l) customs assessment by tariff classification or weight`
`k m` MEANS `(m) deferral or remission of levies`
`k n1` MEANS `(n)(1) nuclear energy: need for a release or for a change of a permit or order`
`k n2` MEANS `(n)(2) nuclear energy: approval of a provisions plan for decommissioning costs`
`k n3` MEANS `(n)(3) nuclear energy: releases`
`k o` MEANS `(o) type approval of road vehicles`
`k p1` MEANS `(p)(1) telecommunications, radio, television and post: concessions`
`k p2` MEANS `(p)(2) telecommunications, radio, television and post: disputes under Art 11a of the Telecommunications Act`
`k p3` MEANS `(p)(3) telecommunications, radio, television and post: disputes under Art 8 of the Postal Act`
`k q1` MEANS `(q)(1) transplantation medicine: entry on the waiting list`
`k q2` MEANS `(q)(2) transplantation medicine: allocation of organs`
`k r` MEANS `(r) health insurance: Federal Administrative Court decision under Art 34 of the Administrative Court Act`
`k s2` MEANS `(s)(2) agriculture: delimitation of the zones of the production cadastre`
`k t` MEANS `(t) results of examinations and other ability assessments`
`k u` MEANS `(u) public takeover offers`
`k v` MEANS `(v) Federal Administrative Court decision on disagreements between authorities in domestic administrative and legal assistance`
`k w` MEANS `(w) electricity law: plan approval of power installations, and expropriation for them`
`k x` MEANS `(x) solidarity contributions for coercive welfare measures and placements before 1981`
`k y` MEANS `(y) Federal Administrative Court decision in a mutual agreement procedure on taxation`
`k z` MEANS `(z) building permits for wind energy installations of national interest`
`k zbis` MEANS `(zbis) water-right concessions for plants under Art 9a(3) of the Electricity Supply Act`
`k zter` MEANS `(zter) complaints by organisations about hydropower plants`
`k none` MEANS `none of these kinds`

§ `Art 82 tests`

#ASSERT `Art 82(a) the appeal in public-law matters lies against the decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82(a) the appeal in public-law matters lies against the decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 82(b) the appeal in public-law matters lies against the cantonal enactment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82(b) the appeal in public-law matters lies against the cantonal enactment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 82(c): args (political voting rights, popular election, popular vote)
#ASSERT `Art 82(c) the appeal in public-law matters lies in a matter of voting rights, popular elections or popular votes` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82(c) the appeal in public-law matters lies in a matter of voting rights, popular elections or popular votes` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82(c) the appeal in public-law matters lies in a matter of voting rights, popular elections or popular votes` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82(c) the appeal in public-law matters lies in a matter of voting rights, popular elections or popular votes` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 82: args (public-law decision, cantonal enactment, voting rights, popular election, popular vote)
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 83 tests: each limb on its own (the first argument says the decision is of the limb's kind)`

-- (a) args (field, international law gives a claim to judicial review): "soweit das Völkerrecht nicht einen Anspruch ... einräumt"
